{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552969-homebrewed-revenants-for-vtm","id":1552969,"title":"Homebrewed Revenants for VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-06T20:55:36-07:00","id":1552969,"title":"Homebrewed Revenants for VTM?","content":"If I asked this before, then I apologized for a retread. But have any you created your own Revenant lineages in your game and and was it hard to pin down a concept and weakness or why a clan would keep them around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T00:58:28-07:00","id":1552973,"title":"","content":"In a sense<br /> Not like the Ventrue Revenants <b>Servants of Anushin-Rawan </b>or the Assamite Sorcerers <b>Kairouan Brotherhood</b> but like the creation of Dr. Douglas Netchurch and his childe Dr. Nancy Reage, the <b>Katayama</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> Actually my Ravenant line was not of human ghouls but of the byproduct of the Nosferatu\u200b Spawning Pools - the Warren accidentally created a Ravenant breed of huge crocodiles and managed to royally piss of a Mokol\u00e9 living nearby becasue they tainted the Mnesis with Nightmares (as flaw)<br /> Thanks to their selective breeding, age and mutation, they were quite inteligent sapient and sentinent - they communciated via hiss and growl and Animalism, had Presence and Potance<br /> It was mostly because one of the players were a Follower of Set, from the <b>Abd'al-Sobek</b> (<i>&quot;Slaves of the Crocodile&quot; </i>) cult and they heard rumors of these &quot;divine beast&quot;, Harbringers of Sobek (the Mokol\u00e9 Abomination 4th Generation child of Sutekh slumbering under the Crocodile Temple, Founding Temple located in Faiyum and had to &quot;save them&quot; from the Nosferatu\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T11:55:38-07:00","id":1552982,"title":"","content":"I am very old school on depicting the Revenants in my chronicles. I hold to their first origin in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand that the Revenant families were created by Verbena belonging to the True Black Hand using vampire vitae. They just don't spontaneously happen if a lot of ghouls breed like they do now. As such there are no &quot;new&quot; Revenant families being created. The secret to their creation has long been lost and vampires simply cannot do it anyway because it requires true Mages.<br /> <br /> However, I do like to fill in mysteries and history gaps in the game. Originally there was supposed to have been eight Revenant families that went into the Sabbat even though only four have survived. So I wanted to know who these families were. They have some value in historical chronicles set in the Dark Ages or Sabbat chronicles prior to the end of the Second Sabbat Civil War. These are my notes for those four Revenant families that entered the Sabbat, but did not survive.<br /> <br /> <b>Ruthvenski</b> - Mentioned in the Libellus Sanguinuis I and revised Clanbook Tzimisce as once existing as a minor Revenant family, but since &quot;absorbed&quot; into other surviving families through intermarriage. I interpret that as a euphemism for them being destroyed while in Sabbat &quot;custody&quot;. The name likely comes from the various Tzimisce that have &quot;Ruthven&quot; in their name. This was likely originally an homage to the fictional character of Lord Ruthven in John Polidori's The Vampyre without the author realizing it is a real Scottish name. The writers eventually realized this and created the &quot;Ruthvenski&quot; which created a more Slavic sounding name to account for all these &quot;Ruthvens&quot; who were embraced as Tzimisce. Presumably these Tzimisce vampires were once Revenants of this line before the embrace. (However, once again it shows the writers kept thinking the Romanians are somehow Slavs when in reality they are a Romance language speaking people who have various Hungarians and Germans people as well. None of these people are Slavs!)<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, the Ruthvenski were destroyed by an internal Sabbat conspiracy during the Second Sabbat Civil War lead by the Lasombra and included the Tremere anti-tribu among others. They didn't particularly trust the Revenant families and wanted to destroy a source of Tzimisce power and influence within the sect.<br /> <br /> <b>Rustovitch</b> - Another family mentioned as having once existed in Libellus Sanguinuis I. The character Vladimir Rustovitch, however, is mentioned as originally being from the Bratovitch. So I am using that as meaning the Rustovitch once existed and entered the Sabbat, but after their destruction their bloodline only exists by prior intermarriage with the Bratovitch. Most likely at a time when the Bratovitch were still nobility and not the degenerate trash they now are.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, the Rustovitch entered the Sabbat, but were destroyed by the Lupines quite early in the history of the Sabbat. They never even made it to the New World. There is a long rivalry between Vladimir Rustovitch and the Lupines, so I wanted to give the Lupines some kind of win to keep Vladimir's enmity ongoing. There may have been a few survivors who were picked off and destroyed by rivals to the Tzimisce within the Sabbat. Any Rustovitch &quot;absorbed&quot; by the Bratovitch had already been married into those families before the family itself was completely wiped out as its own thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Narov</b> - Yet another Revenant family mentioned in the revised Tzimisce clanbook as absorbed into other existing families. So I'm using that as a euphemism that they were one of the original Revenant families to join the Sabbat, but were destroyed with any survivors being taken in by the Obertus. Calling destroyed Revenant families as &quot;minor&quot; is a way to downgrade the perceived loss of that family. So this is the third out of the four destroyed families.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, the Narov were destroyed by a Lasombra conspiracy during the First Sabbat Civil War using the Nosferatu anti-tribu among others as well. This was the start of a long term process by which the Lasombra was targeting something which they saw as a basis of power for their foremost rivals in controlling the Sabbat. Using those allies within the Sabbat who disliked the Tzimisce as well during moments of chaos and violence when Sabbat were already killing each other anyway was one of their tactics.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnamed</b> - There isn't another &quot;minor family&quot; mentioned so I'll have to think of one myself. I haven't yet so they are still currently unnamed. I'd probably use a non-Slavic name, maybe something Italian as the Grimaldi and the Rafastio are associated with Italy, indicating Revenants were present there as well. They are another Revenant family massacred by the Sabbat. This one was less of a concerted conspiracy against this particular family, but more of an opportunistic butchering during the long Second Sabbat Civil War. This was done mostly by Loyalists who disliked the Tzimisce supporting a more centralized sect, and they were orchestrated by the Brujah anti-tribu and their local Ventrue anti-tribu allies. There were also accusations of infernalism and thus the Sabbat Inquisition targeted them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T00:45:44-07:00","id":1553002,"title":"","content":"Take the World of Darkness: Gypsy book and change the name to Vampire the Masquerade: Ravnos Revenants. Bam it makes way more sense now. Its structured pretty much like the Tzimisce families, make the special powers into psuedo disciplines that they start with instead of clan ones, and have them run off blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T21:44:31-07:00","id":1553620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552969-homebrewed-revenants-for-vtm?p=1553002#post1553002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the World of Darkness: Gypsy book and change the name to Vampire the Masquerade: Ravnos Revenants. Bam it makes way more sense now. Its structured pretty much like the Tzimisce families, make the special powers into psuedo disciplines that they start with instead of clan ones, and have them run off blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>kind of</i> did that in a game once, except the &quot;First Tribe&quot; is not at all limited to just romani but nomadic lineages and roving groups spread among cultures across much of the world. And connected to at least one of the supposed origins of the Baali clan/line, so you have them, the Gangrel <i><b>and</b></i> the Ravnos haphazardly duking it out over their fates in the shadows in such a way that no one is even sure of who's at the table, what are the rules or the chips supposed to be anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T22:38:18-07:00","id":1553729,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always liked the idea of Cappadocians/Giovanni having Revenant families of their own. Among those families there would be the Giovanni, Rossellini, Dunsirn, Chalkias, and Pisanob.<br /> <br /> Giovanni and Rossellini are already covered in canon, though my versions are a bit different. Dunsirn, Chalkias, and Pisanob are more of my own creation, at least as Revenant families. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dunsirn</b><br /> A Scottish family of financiers and cannibals, not especially skilled in Necromancy, but skilled combatants and manipulators.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Dominate, Fortitude, Potence<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> Dunsirn revenants do not naturally regain Blood Points, but must consume human flesh to do so. Each human contains 20 Blood Points worth of flesh. For each day dead, a corpse loses 1 BP worth of flesh. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Chalkias</b><br /> A family of scholars and grave robbers who had ties to the Obertus family in addition to serving the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Fortitude, Necromancy, Obfuscate <br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Chalkias family are surrounded by and aura of death and decay. The air is cold in their presence, they smell of earth or rotten flesh, their flesh is sallow and sickly. They suffer a +1 difficulty to all social rolls. This difficulty persists even when they use Obfuscate to disguise their appearance. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pisanob</b><br /> Central American necromancers who combine their ancestral rituals with their mystical Disciplines. <br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Auspex, Necromancy<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Pisanob require the shedding of blood to regain their mystical energies. This need not be consumed, but can be shed in a ritual or sacrifice. In effect, they gain blood points by shedding blood as a vampire dies from drinking blood. Just like a vampire, their BP are reduced by 1BP per day, though they suffer no ill effects when reduced to zero BP. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T17:45:55-07:00","id":1553741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552969-homebrewed-revenants-for-vtm?p=1553729#post1553729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve always liked the idea of Cappadocians/Giovanni having Revenant families of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know.<br /> <br /> While it's not exactly the focus of the thread, I think what VtM is lacking isn't so much more Revenant families, but other categories/rules for servant families that aren't Revenants.<br /> <br /> Revenants aren't a standard mode of servant. They're an experiment, an alchemical work of sorts. Their powers aren't a result of simply being in proximity to vampires or regularly being subject to Ghouling, they're a result of complex and hard to repeat magical intervention. They're less an extension of the clans and more their own things, related to traditional vampires through history, not metaphysics.<br /> <br /> And that isn't necessarily the best take, sure, but it's the take of the game. Making Revenant families based just on the fact of them being servants to vampires just dilute what Revenants are in the setting. There are other possible approaches to this service. Access to Vampire-related Backgrounds and a greater frequency of Ghouls is probably the simplest one, but we can come back with others. There may be a preternatural consequence for long-term familial exposure to vampires. There may not be. But if it is, I don't think it should be as Revenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T23:05:23-07:00","id":1553790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552969-homebrewed-revenants-for-vtm?p=1553741#post1553741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know.<br /> <br /> While it's not exactly the focus of the thread, I think what VtM is lacking isn't so much more Revenant families, but other categories/rules for servant families that aren't Revenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don\u2019t necessarily think that VtM is lacking more Revenant families or lacking anything necessarily. I just think that Revenant families are cool and it\u2019s fun to make more of them and/or make them a bigger part of the setting.<br /> <br /> I can understand not wanting too many Revenant families as they may dilute the concept. Though on the other hand, Giovanni as a Clan and a concept already really play into what the Revenants are, likely more so than the Tzimisce inherently do, and the different subfamilies really lend themselves being being Revenant families. The Giovanni family itself seems like they should be Revenants. <br /> <br /> If you disagree, that\u2019s fine, it\u2019s not going to make anybody accept these new Revenant families or use them in their games. Though the OP did ask, so I\u2019m answering that question. <br /> <br /> I personally don\u2019t like to integrate the different WoD settings, so I reject the idea that Revenants were created by True Magick. I\u2019m then I\u2019m also more open to the possibility of diverse origins for Revenants. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}